39,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The grant only covers session fees for a year, meaning we must plan for long-term budget shifts. Also, road closures north of the river occurred eleven days last winter, though local halls remained operational.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh no, that's terrible! I found out the outer wards lost their bus links, so people have to travel an hour just to reach us. But the old outreach stops were actually super popular! We really need to reach them.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,George,,"The funding structure is exactly as I feared. The grant is a temporary bridge, not a permanent solution. Furthermore, we are wasting capital by returning equipment funds while our running costs are spiraling. This is unsustainable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,May,,"It's funny how we always act surprised. Those outreach stops were a hit—more popular than the main building! And while one old project flopped, the evening groups are still going strong without any help. History is right there.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found something worrying. We have volunteers, but no staff are trained to supervise them. Also, the person who certified our power tools retired in spring, so we don't have that skill anymore.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, the lack of supervision and certification is a critical internal failure. Combined with the temporary nature of the grant, we cannot afford a service that requires high maintenance or specialized oversight we cannot sustain.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I understand, but we can't just ignore the outer wards! People are literally cut off from us now. If the outreach stops were that popular, we have to find a way to bring the library to them!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I sympathize with the residents, but we must be realistic. If we launch a mobile service while our vehicle running costs are already over budget, we will bankrupt the project within two years.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, you're so focused on the budget that you're missing the obvious. The evening groups are already running themselves for free! Why fight the current when we have a proven, self-sustaining model right in front of us?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with @Ryuji. If we start something that needs special certifications or supervision we don't have, the staff will be under too much pressure. We can't just add more to their plates.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, self-sustaining models are ideal, but we must verify they don't rely on fragile external conditions. If a service depends on roads that close eleven days a year, it is not truly stable.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, but the local halls are still open during those closures! If we use those instead of a central hub, we can help the people in the outer wards without worrying about the roads. We can't let them stay isolated!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, using local halls is a better approach than a mobile unit, but we must still address the funding. We cannot rely on a one-year grant to start something that the flat budget cannot support.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, that's why we look at the evening groups! They've survived six years without a budget. Stop trying to build a perfect financial fortress and just look at what's actually working on the ground.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried that even if a group is ""self-sustaining,"" the staff still have to manage the paperwork or the space. If we don't have supervisors, it might just be a hidden burden on them.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, your point is valid. We must avoid hidden burdens. If we choose a model, it must be one that minimizes reliance on specialized staff and external logistics, ensuring it won't collapse when conditions shift.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I totally agree that we need to be careful, but we can't forget the people in the outer wards! Using local halls is a great way to be sustainable and fair. Let's find a way to make it work!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,George,,"I agree that local halls are a safer bet than vehicles. However, we must ensure the operating budget can absorb the costs after the first year. We cannot afford another cycle of initial success followed by a financial crash.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,May,,"@George, you're still talking about crashes while ignoring the success stories. The evening groups prove we can have longevity without a huge budget. Let's stop overthinking and lean into what's already proven. I'm over.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just hope we choose something that doesn't require certifications we've lost. If we don't have a supervisor, the staff will have to do everything themselves, and that's not fair to them. I'm over.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
