64,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option D is too risky given the road closures and vehicle costs. Option C is impossible without tool certification and supervisors. We must choose a model with minimal external dependencies.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I agree about C and D, but we can't just give up on the outer wards! Option A is perfect because it uses community partners and facilitators, meaning we can bring the service to those local halls!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A is the most fiscally responsible choice. It leverages community partners, which reduces our direct operating costs and avoids the budget cliffs associated with high-maintenance infrastructure or vehicle fleets.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,May,,Option A is the only one that actually mirrors the success of those evening groups. It's community-led and sustainable. Option B is just asking for another digitisation disaster like the one from six years ago.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. Option C is too dangerous without the certification, and Option D would be too much for the staff. Option A seems the safest because the facilitators are from the community.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, @George, and @Daisuke, it seems we have reached a consensus. Option A minimizes our reliance on fragile logistics and specialized internal certifications, making it the most stable choice for the long term.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""George"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"I'm so happy we all agree! Option A lets us reach the people in the outer wards who lost their buses, and it does it in a way that's kind to our staff and budget. It's a win-win!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,George,,"It is a relief to find a solution that balances community needs with financial reality. By utilizing partners, we avoid the trap of a temporary grant and ensure the service remains viable long after the first year.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,May,,It's about time we stopped playing it safe and actually looked at the evidence. Option A works because it's a model we know can survive. Let's just get it done before we change our minds.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel much better knowing we aren't choosing something that would overload the staff. Option A seems like the most compassionate choice for everyone involved. I'll vote for that.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. Option A is the only candidate that avoids the vulnerabilities we identified. It is logically the most resilient choice. I will cast my vote for Option A.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
